id: ddp_flash_execution
label: Dynamic Data Provisioning (DDP) Flash execution
description: |
  This component makes the DDP application to be a regular, Flash-based
  application instead of RAM-based. This is required to support devices
  with smaller (RAM) memory. Keep in mind that in this case the Flash will be
  overwritten with the provisioning application, therefore the target
  application needs to be re-programmed.
  DDP uses IO Stream for communication.
package: bluetooth_le
category: Bluetooth|Application|Miscellaneous
quality: production
metadata:
  sbom:
    license: Zlib
root_path: bluetooth_le/common/ddp
provides:
- name: ddp_flash_execution
- name: ddp_execution
requires:
  # For some device families it is not permitted to have an open RTT connection
  # while performing NVM operations. Let's use the recommended (USART/EUSART)
  # IO Stream instance instead.
- name: iostream
  # The default toolchain recommendations do not apply with ddp_ram_execution
  # being recommended. Need to pull directly.
- name: toolchain_gcc_standard
